1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:04,040
♪ I've never believed in love ♪

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:07,400
♪ I've never trusted anyone ♪

3
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:10,080
♪ I've always lived by reason ♪

4
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:14,400
♪ I've never followed my heart ♪

5
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,680
♪ Locked away with a complicated code ♪

6
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:22,040
♪ But you broke through
My heavily guarded firewall ♪

7
00:00:22,040 --> 00:00:26,200
♪ That used to protect my heart ♪

8
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:30,960
♪ I'm in love with you ♪

9
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:34,680
♪ I've just realized today that love ♪

10
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:40,720
♪ Is something I should get to know and explore ♪

11
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:44,080
♪ The code to my heart has been cracked ♪

12
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:48,080
♪ By the love you wrapped me in ♪

13
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:50,840
♪ Having you close puts you in my dreams ♪

14
00:00:50,840 --> 00:00:52,280
♪ You're always on my mind ♪

15
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,880
♪ You cracked my code ♪

16
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:58,080
♪ My heart's security system is disabled ♪

17
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:01,160
♪ You unlocked my heart with a love ♪

18
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:05,960
♪ That this world has never given me ♪

19
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:08,600
♪ Can I write a new code ♪

20
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:11,400
♪ That says I love you? ♪

21
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,080
♪ Love you ♪

22
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:25,200
I'll have Nont handle this campaign.

23
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,680
I know Kit's upset that I didn't listen to him.

24
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:29,000
I hope that by doing this,

25
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,240
he'll see me as more than

26
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:33,280
just his little brother.

27
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,760
If you don't feel it, I'll stop.

28
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,120
Ten years of waiting.

29
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:50,600
It's finally come true.

30
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:53,240
You'll run away from your feelings.

31
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,800
Why do I want to get back up there?

32
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:57,280
What is this feeling?

33
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:02,120
Morning, Kit.

34
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:03,800
Morning.

35
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:11,800
You made coffee for me.

36
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,080
Thank you.

37
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,160
I'm usually a confident person,

38
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,200
both at work and in my personal life.

39
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:23,520
I've always known what I should and shouldn't do.

40
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:27,280
But this morning, I don't know where to start.

41
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,760
Kit, how did you sleep last night?

42
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:33,320
Did you sleep well?

43
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:36,240
Pretty well. I slept soundly.

44
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,200
Me too.

45
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,640
Look, my sleep score is excellent.

46
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,680
About last night...

47
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:52,880
What about it?

48
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,320
You don't remember?

49
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:05,320
All I remember is...

50
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,840
Mr. Roch offered to take me home.

51
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,920
Then everything went black.

52
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:15,160
So did he end up taking me home?

53
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,160
No. I brought you home myself.

54
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:23,080
So what you wanted to know about last night...

55
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:24,840
It's about Roch.

56
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,440
I want you to be careful.

57
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,680
We don't want him finding out about us.

58
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:30,280
Yes, sir.

59
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:35,200
I won't slip up next time.

60
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:40,120
Want something to eat? I'll make you some toast.

61
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,640
Okay?

62
00:03:47,320 --> 00:03:49,160
Are you really that relieved

63
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:51,640
that I said I don't remember?

64
00:03:52,640 --> 00:03:54,160
What if I told you I do?

65
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:56,920
I remember everything.

66
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:01,160
I even remember...

67
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,880
how happy you were.

68
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,560
He doesn't remember.

69
00:04:07,880 --> 00:04:10,280
Then consider nothing happened last night.

70
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:12,920
That's for the best.

71
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,480
What's there to think about?

72
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,920
You don't have to make anything.

73
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:22,600
I'm not hungry.

74
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,040
If you want to run, go ahead.

75
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:29,960
But I won't run.

76
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:31,880
I'll wait

77
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:34,960
until you're ready to accept

78
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:39,320
that I'm no longer just your little brother.

79
00:04:59,680 --> 00:05:01,480
Kit, I made pasta.

80
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:04,520
I'm fasting every day now. I'm off to work.

81
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:07,080
Kit.

82
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,920
You've had enough booze.

83
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:23,680
Ready to talk now?

84
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,040
What's going on? Tell me.

85
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:30,120
Remember the night of the party?

86
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,400
I was drunk, right?

87
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,480
I went home.

88
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:39,240
And then Kit and I...

89
00:05:39,640 --> 00:05:40,600
kissed.

90
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,040
And then...

91
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,040
After you kissed...

92
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:48,400
Did you and Kit...

93
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,720
No, no, no. It's not like that.

94
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:54,440
We didn't have actual sex.

95
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,360
We just...

96
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:57,680
Well...

97
00:05:58,120 --> 00:06:00,160
Took matters into your own hands?

98
00:06:03,320 --> 00:06:04,840
You little shit.

99
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:07,520
Yeah, exactly.

100
00:06:10,840 --> 00:06:13,760
Nont, I'm happy for you, man.

101
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:16,360
You finally got to try it.

102
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:20,560
I mean... I'm kind of happy, too.

103
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:23,440
So why the hell are you sitting here moping?

104
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:28,040
I thought he'd finally seen me for who I am.

105
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:31,840
But...

106
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:34,280
when morning came...

107
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,200
he was scared of me.

108
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:40,040
He asked if I remembered.

109
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:42,640
About last night...

110
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,760
What about it?

111
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,200
You don't remember?

112
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,440
Of course not, Kit.

113
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:47,720
I was way too drunk.

114
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,280
Good.

115
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:52,360
So I told him I didn't remember.

116
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:53,800
Shit.

117
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:57,160
I lied to him because I wanted him to feel better.

118
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,320
What did he say?

119
00:06:58,920 --> 00:07:00,200
He said,

120
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:01,800
"Good."

121
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:06,120
But I do remember.

122
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:09,320
I remember everything, Sharp.

123
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:11,280
I remember how he started.

124
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:14,800
How he touched me.

125
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:16,480
How he kissed me.

126
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:20,040
I remember every second, every touch.

127
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,800
I remember everything.

128
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:26,960
I just don't know what's wrong with him.

129
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,560
Kit.

130
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:31,000
Why haven't you read my messages?

131
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,360
I was busy with a client.

132
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,560
I'm going to bed.

133
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:35,520
Kit...

134
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,200
After that, he kept walking away and ignoring me.

135
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:42,760
He wouldn't reply to my messages or eat with me.

136
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,880
Stay.

137
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,440
I left something in your room.

138
00:07:55,360 --> 00:07:58,440
We pass each other at home,
and he treats me like a stranger, Sharp.

139
00:07:58,440 --> 00:07:59,560
Shit.

140
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:03,080
I don't know if he finds me disgusting, Sharp.

141
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:06,760
Or if he just regrets what he did

142
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:08,600
and wants to forget it.

143
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:12,360
Nont, I get how you feel, man.

144
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:14,200
Am I stupid, Sharp?

145
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:15,920
Huh?

146
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:18,680
Tell me, am I stupid for...

147
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:21,360
waiting for someone who doesn't even see me?

148
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:25,920
Nont.

149
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
You're not stupid.

150
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,440
You're just in love.

151
00:08:34,560 --> 00:08:36,040
But tell me the truth.

152
00:08:36,040 --> 00:08:38,440
How much longer are you gonna wait for him?

153
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:40,680
I'm not telling you to stop loving him.

154
00:08:40,680 --> 00:08:42,960
I just want you to love yourself, too.

155
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,640
You've been hurting because of Kit

156
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:47,240
since we were in school.

157
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:50,560
Whenever he had a girlfriend, you'd end up crying.

158
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,240
As your friend,

159
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,560
I want you to know

160
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,640
that no matter how Kit feels,

161
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,760
you'll always matter.

162
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:03,160
Don't let anyone make you feel like you don't.

163
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:07,800
I think...

164
00:09:08,160 --> 00:09:09,640
Thanks, man, but...

165
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:11,280
- It's okay.
- You don't have to.

166
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:14,120
I... I... I think I'm okay now.

167
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,560
Go try that on someone else.

168
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:21,000
I don't wanna see it.

169
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:26,600
Nont, how's it going?

170
00:09:27,360 --> 00:09:28,800
Settling in with the team?

171
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:30,720
Yes, I am.

172
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:32,560
Everyone's been really nice.

173
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:37,000
I called you in today to tell you that

174
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:39,440
I'm making you my assistant.

175
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:42,600
Uh, what would my duties be?

176
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:46,040
Everything I do, and everything
I don't have time to do.

177
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:47,880
I have a degree in marketing.

178
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:51,280
Sharp's the same age as you.
He also has a degree in marketing.

179
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:53,640
Kit still made him his assistant.

180
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:58,600
But if you're not sure, you can think it over.

181
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:00,840
But if you say yes,

182
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:03,440
think about your salary and let me know.

183
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:05,040
I will.

184
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,240
That's all I wanted to discuss.

185
00:10:07,680 --> 00:10:11,320
Oh, and get someone out there
to help pack up my office.

186
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:15,840
That's okay.

187
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,440
I'll help you.

188
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:18,920
Alright, sure.

189
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,360
You sent for me, boss?

190
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,400
How's Nont doing lately?

191
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:32,240
I haven't talked to him much lately.
He's busy preparing for the office move.

192
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:34,800
When are they moving in?

193
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:37,680
I'm not sure yet. Probably in another week or so.

194
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,640
Has he told you anything lately?

195
00:10:43,760 --> 00:10:45,120
Like what, boss?

196
00:10:49,280 --> 00:10:50,680
About his job at RC.

197
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,840
Has he had any problems?

198
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:55,360
Not that I know of.

199
00:10:55,840 --> 00:10:57,640
That's all. Thanks.

200
00:10:58,800 --> 00:10:59,680
Yes, boss.

201
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,400
(I love you, my sweet boy)

202
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,360
"Love"?

203
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:47,880
Almost done?

204
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:50,080
Ow.

205
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:51,200
Whoa.

206
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:52,680
You're bleeding.

207
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:55,360
It's not deep. Just a little cut.

208
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,400
It's pretty deep.

209
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:57,680
Wait a second.

210
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:15,200
Your hands are important. Be careful.

211
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:18,160
Thank you.

212
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,080
Oh, those photos are really old.

213
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:27,880
Did you and Kit go to school together, Mr. Roch?

214
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,680
We studied abroad together.

215
00:12:31,920 --> 00:12:34,200
You're really not staying
to further your studies?

216
00:12:34,720 --> 00:12:36,440
I can put in a good word for you.

217
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:38,600
Thank you.

218
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:41,400
But I'm planning to go home after my exams.

219
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:44,040
Is someone waiting for you back home?

220
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:45,200
Yes.

221
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,800
Who is it? Can you tell me?

222
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:50,520
My little brother.

223
00:12:50,840 --> 00:12:54,200
He's waiting for me.
He even asked me to bring him a souvenir.

224
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:57,120
Are you two very close?

225
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:02,240
Yes. He's not my biological brother,
but we're really close.

226
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,400
I'm really gonna miss you, Kit.

227
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,280
We go out every night.

228
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,520
Who am I gonna hang out with now?

229
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:16,360
Are you gonna miss me, too?

230
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:22,840
Are you drunk, Roch?

231
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,360
Do I look drunk?

232
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,240
Let's keep walking. It's late.

233
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:35,160
Kit and I met while pursuing
our master's degrees in the US.

234
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:38,120
Kit never told me about this.

235
00:13:38,760 --> 00:13:40,000
I'm not surprised.

236
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,920
Things didn't end well between us.

237
00:13:44,680 --> 00:13:46,080
I loved Kit back then.

238
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:48,960
Romantically.

239
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,680
Not just as a close friend.

240
00:13:52,760 --> 00:13:55,440
How do you feel about him now, Mr. Roch?

241
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,360
Unrequited love.

242
00:13:58,600 --> 00:14:00,680
Over time, it turned into something else.

243
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,760
What about you?

244
00:14:04,720 --> 00:14:06,160
Are you in love with someone

245
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:09,280
you've waited for so long,
but who's never noticed you?

246
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:13,680
Uh...

247
00:14:15,880 --> 00:14:16,840
Well, I...

248
00:14:16,840 --> 00:14:17,840
Nont.

249
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,240
Let me tell you something.

250
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:21,920
Waiting for someone your whole life

251
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:24,360
doesn't mean you're strong.

252
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:27,400
Sometimes, you're just afraid.

253
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,640
Afraid to walk away.

254
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,840
I've been there.

255
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:31,800
Trust me.

256
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:36,040
It's not as scary as you think.

257
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:16,560
Nice house.

258
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:21,280
Mr. Roch,

259
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:24,200
I'm sorry I can't invite you inside.

260
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,040
It's totally fine.

261
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:30,000
Even if you did, I wouldn't go in.

262
00:15:30,480 --> 00:15:33,200
I know Kit doesn't like people
meddling in his personal life.

263
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:35,720
Thank you.

264
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,080
About what I told you today,

265
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:40,040
you don't have to tell him.

266
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:43,560
Okay.

267
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:49,520
Go on, get some rest.

268
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:51,560
I'll see you tomorrow.

269
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:53,560
Sure.

270
00:16:28,440 --> 00:16:30,200
Oh, you're back.

271
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:34,560
You're still up.

272
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:36,240
Waiting for me?

273
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:37,760
No.

274
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:40,040
I was hungry, so I ordered some food.

275
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,280
I ordered some for you, too.

276
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:45,040
Thank you, but I already ate.

277
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:52,440
Next time, let me know, so I don't order extra.

278
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:53,800
Is something bothering you?

279
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,920
No.

280
00:16:55,840 --> 00:16:57,000
Did I do something wrong?

281
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:05,880
Good night.

282
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:15,640
Kit, I know you were waiting for me.

283
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,320
I wasn't. You're overthinking it.

284
00:17:19,480 --> 00:17:21,680
Why can't you be honest with me?

285
00:17:28,680 --> 00:17:29,760
About what?

286
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:31,440
Everything.

287
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:34,200
What's bothering you,

288
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,120
or how you really feel.

289
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:40,040
How I feel is my business, not yours.

290
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,040
Exactly.

291
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:44,800
That's so you. You've always been like this.

292
00:18:03,160 --> 00:18:04,440
I'm tired.

293
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,640
Tired of what?

294
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,160
Tired of having to guess.

295
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,640
Tired of reading between the lines.

296
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:14,120
I'm tired of you never being honest with me.

297
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:17,920
Do you have any idea

298
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:21,040
how long I've been waiting for you?

299
00:18:24,320 --> 00:18:26,440
I've been waiting for you to see me.

300
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,520
Not as your little brother,

301
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,400
but as my own person.

302
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,840
What are you saying?

303
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:33,880
You heard me.

304
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:37,040
Ten years, Kit.

305
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:40,840
I've loved you for ten years.

306
00:18:41,520 --> 00:18:42,600
But you had no idea

307
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:44,680
because you never really saw me.

308
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:46,920
Nont, it's impossible.

309
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:48,200
Why is it impossible?

310
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:51,080
Because we're both men?

311
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,240
Or are you just afraid?

312
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,280
We're brothers, Nont.

313
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:01,320
We've never been brothers, Kit.

314
00:19:02,920 --> 00:19:05,720
We have never been brothers.

315
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,520
Do you understand?

316
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:12,040
We've never been brothers. Not to me!

317
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,920
You don't have to give me an answer today.

318
00:19:34,920 --> 00:19:37,160
But I can't keep waiting without hope.

319
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:04,520
I'll sleep in the study.

320
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,480
I don't know if I'll lose you,

321
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:27,000
but I can't bear being just your brother anymore.

322
00:21:27,840 --> 00:21:29,200
I loved Kit back then.

323
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,280
Romantically.

324
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:32,840
Not just as a close friend.

325
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:34,680
What about Kit?

326
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:36,280
He didn't know.

327
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:40,120
Or maybe he did, but didn't want to
acknowledge it. I'm not sure.

328
00:21:41,120 --> 00:21:42,720
I'm not sure either.

329
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,120
Mr. Roch was right.

330
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:51,320
Waiting for someone your whole life
doesn't mean you're strong.

331
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:54,520
You're just afraid to move forward.

332
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:57,360
I'm done being afraid now.

333
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:04,840
Even someone I just met

334
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:07,280
can see that I'm hurt.

335
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:11,280
But the person I've waited ten years for

336
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,480
has never even noticed the wound on my hand.

337
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,800
You told me you loved me.

338
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,040
I wasn't shocked.

339
00:22:36,840 --> 00:22:37,880
I was scared.

340
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:42,120
I was scared that if I reciprocated,
everything would change.

341
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:43,520
I was scared I'd hurt you.

342
00:22:44,520 --> 00:22:47,480
Or I was scared that if I actually loved you,

343
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:51,240
I'd have to accept who I really am.

344
00:24:43,901 --> 00:24:45,341
Am I dreaming?

345
00:24:45,341 --> 00:24:48,141
Nont, I made fried rice
with Chinese sausage for you.

346
00:24:48,141 --> 00:24:49,061
Come sit down.

347
00:25:00,061 --> 00:25:01,181
Give it a try.

348
00:25:10,581 --> 00:25:11,421
How is it?

349
00:25:15,021 --> 00:25:18,501
It's pretty good. It'd be perfect
with a little Maggi seasoning sauce.

350
00:25:24,061 --> 00:25:27,101
You love salty food.
You'll end up with kidney disease.

351
00:25:29,461 --> 00:25:32,861
You know, men like us struggle to find
someone to care for us when we're old.

352
00:25:33,981 --> 00:25:34,901
Uh...

353
00:25:35,461 --> 00:25:37,501
I mean, men who work as hard as we do.

354
00:25:39,021 --> 00:25:39,981
I see.

355
00:25:41,981 --> 00:25:42,981
Right.

356
00:25:46,141 --> 00:25:47,541
Sit down and eat with me?

357
00:25:58,061 --> 00:26:00,781
I'm free today. I can drive you to the office.

358
00:26:15,821 --> 00:26:16,621
Nont.

359
00:26:18,181 --> 00:26:21,061
I've been thinking about what happened last night.

360
00:26:24,981 --> 00:26:26,461
I need some time.

361
00:26:30,101 --> 00:26:32,021
But while we're living together,

362
00:26:33,181 --> 00:26:35,141
could you not bring it up again?

363
00:26:37,781 --> 00:26:40,861
When I'm ready, I'll give you an answer.

364
00:26:43,141 --> 00:26:44,101
I understand.

365
00:26:45,381 --> 00:26:46,621
I'll go get dressed, then.

366
00:26:47,541 --> 00:26:48,981
Then I'll drive you to work.

367
00:26:52,101 --> 00:26:53,141
Eat up.

368
00:26:58,261 --> 00:27:00,941
Kit, I've waited a long time.

369
00:27:01,661 --> 00:27:05,301
But this time, you've given me hope.

370
00:27:12,061 --> 00:27:14,981
If I'd taken the SkyTrain,
you wouldn't be stuck in traffic.

371
00:27:15,741 --> 00:27:17,821
It's fine. I'm not in a hurry.

372
00:27:18,941 --> 00:27:21,061
So, when are you gonna start driving?

373
00:27:22,501 --> 00:27:23,821
No way, Kit.

374
00:27:24,301 --> 00:27:26,141
I'd rather take a rideshare.

375
00:27:28,221 --> 00:27:29,181
Nont.

376
00:27:30,101 --> 00:27:32,381
Roch told you about me and him, didn't he?

377
00:27:36,461 --> 00:27:38,021
How did you know, Kit?

378
00:27:38,781 --> 00:27:40,181
I know Roch well.

379
00:27:41,701 --> 00:27:43,941
If you're curious about Roch,

380
00:27:43,941 --> 00:27:45,021
just ask me.

381
00:27:45,981 --> 00:27:47,821
I'd rather you hear it from me.

382
00:27:49,381 --> 00:27:50,541
Well,

383
00:27:51,501 --> 00:27:53,661
if there's anything you want me to know,

384
00:27:53,661 --> 00:27:54,781
just tell me.

385
00:27:56,181 --> 00:27:57,981
I've known Roch for a long time.

386
00:28:00,061 --> 00:28:01,781
He once told me...

387
00:28:03,421 --> 00:28:04,301
he loved me.

388
00:28:05,141 --> 00:28:07,301
You're really not staying
to further your studies?

389
00:28:07,301 --> 00:28:09,581
I'll quit my PhD and go back with you.

390
00:28:10,221 --> 00:28:11,101
Please?

391
00:28:15,541 --> 00:28:16,581
I love you, Kit.

392
00:28:18,301 --> 00:28:19,581
I love you so much.

393
00:28:19,901 --> 00:28:21,821
I don't feel that way about you.

394
00:28:22,181 --> 00:28:23,421
Just give me a chance.

395
00:28:27,701 --> 00:28:28,821
Roch, stop!

396
00:28:33,461 --> 00:28:35,141
So, did you turn him down

397
00:28:35,901 --> 00:28:38,021
because he's a man?

398
00:28:39,141 --> 00:28:40,581
That's not how I see it.

399
00:28:41,821 --> 00:28:43,501
Even if Roch were a woman,

400
00:28:44,141 --> 00:28:45,821
I'd still have done the same.

401
00:28:46,861 --> 00:28:48,301
Then...

402
00:28:48,301 --> 00:28:49,501
what...

403
00:28:50,341 --> 00:28:52,061
kind of guy do you like?

404
00:28:53,301 --> 00:28:56,861
Honestly, I don't mind men
confessing their love to me.

405
00:28:57,741 --> 00:29:01,141
I just didn't feel that way about Roch.

406
00:29:02,341 --> 00:29:06,941
Then what kind of guy
would you feel that way about?

407
00:29:08,461 --> 00:29:10,581
I'm still figuring that out myself.

408
00:29:17,781 --> 00:29:20,301
Thank you for being honest with me.

409
00:29:31,061 --> 00:29:34,941
♪ When closeness starts to stir up feelings ♪

410
00:29:34,941 --> 00:29:42,101
♪ And my heart starts to get carried away ♪

411
00:29:42,101 --> 00:29:45,781
♪ As our bond begins to change ♪

412
00:29:45,781 --> 00:29:47,861
♪ Every time I look at you ♪

413
00:29:47,861 --> 00:29:50,421
♪ My heart ♪

414
00:29:50,861 --> 00:29:53,981
♪ Flutters more than I can bear ♪

415
00:29:54,621 --> 00:29:57,261
♪ Before I knew it ♪

416
00:29:57,261 --> 00:30:01,141
♪ Before I realized how I felt
I couldn't stop it anymore ♪

417
00:30:01,141 --> 00:30:02,621
I hope you find yourself.

418
00:30:03,301 --> 00:30:06,621
♪ It's too late now ♪

419
00:30:06,621 --> 00:30:12,141
♪ I'm already yours ♪

420
00:30:14,141 --> 00:30:17,341
♪ Somehow I gave my heart to you ♪

421
00:30:17,821 --> 00:30:23,501
♪ I don't even know when it happened ♪

422
00:30:24,861 --> 00:30:28,221
♪ Someone who's always here ♪

423
00:30:28,221 --> 00:30:33,181
♪ Someone you know so well ♪

424
00:30:33,621 --> 00:30:38,461
♪ There's something I've been waiting to say ♪

425
00:30:43,821 --> 00:30:46,461
Welcome, everyone from RC Capital.

426
00:30:46,461 --> 00:30:49,581
We all know each other,
so no need for introductions, right?

427
00:30:49,581 --> 00:30:51,141
But I do need to make one.

428
00:30:51,581 --> 00:30:54,141
I'd like to introduce
my new assistant, Mr. Nontawat.

429
00:30:54,541 --> 00:30:55,341
Yes.

430
00:30:58,021 --> 00:31:01,501
If you need to reach me, just go through him.

431
00:31:14,461 --> 00:31:15,621
Is your wound healed?

432
00:31:17,461 --> 00:31:19,101
You just lifted a heavy box.

433
00:31:19,101 --> 00:31:20,181
It is.

434
00:31:22,461 --> 00:31:24,941
Mr. Nont, I need to talk to you.

435
00:31:26,581 --> 00:31:27,381
Sure.

436
00:31:28,661 --> 00:31:31,101
Mr. Roch, excuse me for a moment.

437
00:31:33,701 --> 00:31:34,741
Hey.

438
00:31:35,501 --> 00:31:36,381
Kit.

439
00:31:39,741 --> 00:31:40,941
What's up, Kit?

440
00:31:41,541 --> 00:31:42,461
Nothing.

441
00:31:42,821 --> 00:31:43,621
Eh?

442
00:31:43,621 --> 00:31:45,181
Stay here. Go back in later.

443
00:31:46,661 --> 00:31:47,621
Uh...

444
00:32:08,301 --> 00:32:09,981
I need tomorrow's schedule.

445
00:32:22,141 --> 00:32:23,901
Nont, let's get lunch.

446
00:32:24,461 --> 00:32:26,421
- Oh...
- I already have plans with Nont.

447
00:32:27,981 --> 00:32:28,821
Huh?

448
00:32:28,821 --> 00:32:31,581
We have to run an errand
for my mom after lunch, too.

449
00:32:32,501 --> 00:32:34,181
- Huh?
- Stop saying "huh."

450
00:32:34,181 --> 00:32:35,901
Come on. We'll be late getting back.

451
00:32:38,901 --> 00:32:39,861
Uh...

452
00:32:42,261 --> 00:32:45,661
Mr. Roch, you'll have to excuse me.

453
00:32:45,661 --> 00:32:48,261
Go ahead. I'm not holding you here.

454
00:33:11,181 --> 00:33:12,581
Pulling me away again.

455
00:33:12,581 --> 00:33:14,941
Kit, we didn't make plans.

456
00:33:15,901 --> 00:33:17,221
We're making them now.

457
00:33:17,701 --> 00:33:19,501
Let's make it a standing date.

458
00:33:19,501 --> 00:33:23,101
Every day at lunch,
unless I have to meet a client,

459
00:33:23,101 --> 00:33:25,061
you have to eat lunch with me.

460
00:33:30,981 --> 00:33:32,381
Are you jealous, Kit?

461
00:33:32,381 --> 00:33:33,341
I'm not jealous.

462
00:33:36,181 --> 00:33:38,021
You're my brother. I'm just worried.

463
00:33:40,541 --> 00:33:41,541
Brother again.

464
00:33:41,861 --> 00:33:44,781
Kit, stop calling me your brother.

465
00:33:44,781 --> 00:33:46,061
Just call me Nont.

466
00:33:46,581 --> 00:33:48,541
Then you stop calling me that, too.

467
00:33:48,541 --> 00:33:50,301
I do that out of respect.

468
00:33:50,981 --> 00:33:53,861
What, do you want me
to call you "boss" like Sharp does?

469
00:33:53,861 --> 00:33:54,661
No.

470
00:33:55,781 --> 00:33:56,741
Fine.

471
00:33:56,741 --> 00:33:58,661
I'll stop calling you my brother.

472
00:33:58,661 --> 00:33:59,741
I'll just call you Nont.

473
00:34:00,181 --> 00:34:01,181
Thank you.

474
00:34:56,084 --> 00:34:57,724
How is it? Taste good?

475
00:34:58,484 --> 00:35:00,804
It's interesting. My first time trying it.

476
00:35:01,244 --> 00:35:03,404
Anyway, what did you wanna talk about?

477
00:35:05,004 --> 00:35:06,044
Well...

478
00:35:07,124 --> 00:35:08,324
Kit really confuses me.

479
00:35:09,164 --> 00:35:12,604
All of a sudden, he's been
paying a lot more attention to me.

480
00:35:14,244 --> 00:35:16,564
Maybe he's finally realizing his feelings.

481
00:35:16,564 --> 00:35:17,764
I'm sure he hasn't.

482
00:35:19,924 --> 00:35:23,284
Hey, I'm gonna be blunt.
Who made the first move that night?

483
00:35:26,724 --> 00:35:28,164
Why do you wanna know?

484
00:35:29,164 --> 00:35:30,244
I'm just curious.

485
00:35:30,724 --> 00:35:31,564
Tell me.

486
00:35:33,124 --> 00:35:34,004
Kit did.

487
00:35:35,004 --> 00:35:36,244
I'm just making sure.

488
00:35:37,484 --> 00:35:38,884
Then let me sum it up.

489
00:35:38,884 --> 00:35:41,244
Kit's a top, and you're a bottom.

490
00:35:41,964 --> 00:35:43,804
Because you and I are the same.

491
00:35:46,684 --> 00:35:48,644
You're good at this stuff, huh?

492
00:35:49,004 --> 00:35:50,404
So, how was he?

493
00:35:50,404 --> 00:35:52,764
When he kissed and touched you,

494
00:35:53,164 --> 00:35:54,404
was he really good?

495
00:35:55,244 --> 00:35:57,844
What kind of question is that?
Why do you wanna know?

496
00:35:58,604 --> 00:36:00,124
It's important, man.

497
00:36:00,124 --> 00:36:01,124
Just tell me.

498
00:36:02,604 --> 00:36:03,484
Come on.

499
00:36:10,364 --> 00:36:12,284
He was pretty good at kissing.

500
00:36:12,284 --> 00:36:13,084
Huh?

501
00:36:13,084 --> 00:36:15,484
He was so good that I...

502
00:36:16,324 --> 00:36:17,924
could barely breathe.

503
00:36:19,364 --> 00:36:21,484
But when it came to...

504
00:36:21,484 --> 00:36:23,364
touching me down there...

505
00:36:26,204 --> 00:36:29,764
I think he was just acting on instinct.

506
00:36:31,644 --> 00:36:32,524
Aha!

507
00:36:33,044 --> 00:36:33,964
I get it now.

508
00:36:33,964 --> 00:36:35,404
Here's my conclusion.

509
00:36:35,404 --> 00:36:37,084
Kit's a late bloomer.

510
00:36:37,364 --> 00:36:38,124
What's that?

511
00:36:38,124 --> 00:36:39,884
He blooms late.

512
00:36:40,084 --> 00:36:42,284
He takes longer to figure out what he's into.

513
00:36:42,284 --> 00:36:46,364
That's why he needs a little help
to figure himself out sooner.

514
00:36:46,724 --> 00:36:47,724
What kind of help?

515
00:36:47,724 --> 00:36:48,804
Porn.

516
00:36:49,244 --> 00:36:50,204
Porn?

517
00:36:51,684 --> 00:36:52,804
Watch it with him.

518
00:36:53,364 --> 00:36:54,524
Are you crazy?

519
00:36:55,044 --> 00:36:56,844
How am I supposed to do that?

520
00:36:56,844 --> 00:36:58,804
He asked me for more time.

521
00:36:58,804 --> 00:37:00,364
I don't want to pressure him.

522
00:37:00,364 --> 00:37:03,244
Then watch it in secret, but make sure he sees.

523
00:37:03,244 --> 00:37:06,084
Let him see what sex between two men looks like.

524
00:37:06,564 --> 00:37:09,644
There's nothing weird about two men having sex.

525
00:37:10,804 --> 00:37:13,444
Sometimes the body knows before the mind does.

526
00:37:13,844 --> 00:37:16,524
Is that what you do with your boyfriends?

527
00:37:19,244 --> 00:37:20,364
All of them.

528
00:37:21,524 --> 00:37:24,164
We're gay. No one teaches us this stuff.

529
00:37:24,604 --> 00:37:25,684
We learn as we go.

530
00:37:27,004 --> 00:37:29,124
Alright, I'll send you a link, okay?

531
00:37:30,924 --> 00:37:32,764
What kind of friend are you?

532
00:37:33,524 --> 00:37:35,444
The kind who loves you dearly.

533
00:37:37,244 --> 00:37:38,284
Go for it.

534
00:37:53,084 --> 00:37:55,684
Sharp told me to watch it in secret,

535
00:37:56,564 --> 00:37:57,884
but make sure Kit sees.

536
00:38:23,604 --> 00:38:24,964
Nont, I'm home!

537
00:38:30,724 --> 00:38:31,564
What's this?

538
00:38:32,844 --> 00:38:33,724
Porn.

539
00:38:36,564 --> 00:38:38,404
I know it's porn, but why are they...

540
00:38:38,404 --> 00:38:40,644
Why? Why are they both men?

541
00:38:42,044 --> 00:38:45,124
Kit, I like men. Did you expect me to watch women?

542
00:38:46,284 --> 00:38:47,044
Turn it off.

543
00:38:47,044 --> 00:38:48,044
No.

544
00:38:48,044 --> 00:38:48,964
What did you say?

545
00:38:48,964 --> 00:38:50,204
I said no.

546
00:38:51,084 --> 00:38:53,204
If you don't wanna watch, you can leave.

547
00:38:54,044 --> 00:38:55,084
Turn it off, Nont.

548
00:38:58,044 --> 00:38:59,044
No.

549
00:38:59,284 --> 00:39:01,244
Nont, give it here. I'll do it.

550
00:39:01,244 --> 00:39:02,044
Hey.

551
00:39:02,044 --> 00:39:03,364
Whoa.

552
00:39:03,364 --> 00:39:04,484
- What, Kit?
- Nont.

553
00:39:05,564 --> 00:39:06,924
- Kit.
- Nont.

554
00:39:06,924 --> 00:39:07,724
Kit.

555
00:39:16,164 --> 00:39:18,004
Do you feel what I feel, Kit?

556
00:39:21,364 --> 00:39:22,684
Sharp was right.

557
00:39:23,644 --> 00:39:28,204
Sometimes the body knows before the mind does.

558
00:39:38,724 --> 00:39:40,204
Let's take this to the bedroom.

559
00:39:48,524 --> 00:39:49,644
I don't know how.

560
00:39:50,764 --> 00:39:51,604
It's okay.

561
00:39:54,324 --> 00:39:55,444
Just follow my lead.

562
00:39:59,764 --> 00:40:01,444
I want you to see me

563
00:40:02,724 --> 00:40:04,484
as more than your little brother.

564
00:40:09,644 --> 00:40:11,684
I've seen you since you were a kid.

565
00:40:12,764 --> 00:40:13,844
So why...

566
00:40:14,844 --> 00:40:17,724
is my heart beating so fast right now?

567
00:40:27,804 --> 00:40:29,244
I want to see you, too.

568
00:40:51,044 --> 00:40:52,164
What now?

569
00:41:05,444 --> 00:41:07,084
You don't have to change anything.

570
00:41:08,364 --> 00:41:09,804
Just be yourself, Kit.

571
00:41:12,244 --> 00:41:13,244
I'm scared.

572
00:41:16,684 --> 00:41:18,204
I'm afraid I'll do it wrong.

573
00:41:19,684 --> 00:41:21,044
How about you kiss me?

574
00:42:21,764 --> 00:42:23,124
Can you hold me, Kit?

575
00:42:39,364 --> 00:42:40,324
I'm ready now.

576
00:43:09,124 --> 00:43:10,324
Did you like it?

577
00:43:11,124 --> 00:43:12,644
I'm not sure if I liked it.

578
00:43:14,844 --> 00:43:16,164
But I didn't want it to end.

579
00:43:20,684 --> 00:43:21,764
Why are you smiling?

580
00:43:26,524 --> 00:43:27,724
I'm just happy.

581
00:44:36,377 --> 00:44:38,537
Get your boss to the office ASAP.

582
00:44:38,537 --> 00:44:39,737
What's so urgent, sir?

583
00:44:39,737 --> 00:44:43,577
Something that could put our company
on the map and send our stock soaring.

584
00:44:43,577 --> 00:44:44,617
What's the gist, sir?

585
00:44:45,057 --> 00:44:48,417
Tell Kit we've secured an investor from the US.

586
00:44:49,657 --> 00:44:52,177
But we have to decide within 24 hours.

587
00:44:52,817 --> 00:44:53,617
Got it, sir.

588
00:45:27,817 --> 00:45:28,857
Hello. What's up?

589
00:45:29,217 --> 00:45:30,857
Boss, it's urgent.

590
00:45:30,857 --> 00:45:32,297
Mr. Roch called.

591
00:45:32,297 --> 00:45:36,737
An investor from the US
has given us 24 hours to decide.

592
00:45:38,697 --> 00:45:39,977
Okay, I'm on my way.

593
00:45:44,577 --> 00:45:45,857
I know it's Saturday.

594
00:45:45,857 --> 00:45:48,457
I'll take you out to eat after this meeting, okay?

595
00:45:50,937 --> 00:45:52,337
Mm, okay.

596
00:46:11,417 --> 00:46:13,057
Can we do this every day?

597
00:46:23,137 --> 00:46:24,577
(Kittipat Auttawarakul's Vision for Turning
No Secret Lab into a Leading Software House)

598
00:46:24,577 --> 00:46:27,977
If you think Kit is just lucky,
born into a wealthy family,

599
00:46:27,977 --> 00:46:29,977
and that's how he's gotten to where he is,

600
00:46:30,737 --> 00:46:31,937
you're wrong.

601
00:46:32,697 --> 00:46:35,097
He wasn't just born with a head start.

602
00:46:35,657 --> 00:46:37,577
He's a man with a dream,

603
00:46:38,417 --> 00:46:40,097
a dream others can't keep up with.

604
00:46:43,177 --> 00:46:46,217
His company rose to prominence
at an incredible pace.

605
00:46:46,977 --> 00:46:50,537
And none of this happened because of luck,

606
00:46:50,537 --> 00:46:52,257
but because of hard work.

607
00:46:53,417 --> 00:46:55,337
In the eyes of investors,

608
00:46:55,857 --> 00:46:59,897
Kit is a top-tier young businessman
who's practically perfect,

609
00:47:00,217 --> 00:47:01,857
and seemingly out of reach.

610
00:47:02,177 --> 00:47:06,777
But right now, in this moment,
I've finally reached him.

611
00:47:09,657 --> 00:47:10,617
What's wrong?

612
00:47:12,657 --> 00:47:14,137
I'm just a lucky man.

613
00:47:28,577 --> 00:47:30,697
I got sent these two photos last night.

614
00:47:30,697 --> 00:47:31,497
Is it true?

615
00:47:31,497 --> 00:47:33,577
Did you and Boss really get married?

616
00:47:35,177 --> 00:47:36,577
I love you.

617
00:47:36,897 --> 00:47:38,937
But I have to make a decision.

618
00:47:39,977 --> 00:47:41,257
Lately...

619
00:47:41,817 --> 00:47:44,097
I've been the happiest I've ever been.

620
00:47:44,097 --> 00:47:47,817
Photos have surfaced
showing that your spouse is a man.

621
00:47:47,817 --> 00:47:48,737
It's true.

622
00:47:49,537 --> 00:47:51,617
That's right. It's nothing.

623
00:47:51,617 --> 00:47:54,817
When you said
there was nothing serious between us,

624
00:47:55,297 --> 00:47:56,617
did you mean it?

625
00:47:56,617 --> 00:47:58,977
You chose the company! You chose money!

626
00:47:59,777 --> 00:48:01,097
I didn't choose!

627
00:48:01,097 --> 00:48:03,617
I want someone who'll stand by me,

628
00:48:03,617 --> 00:48:05,617
not someone who'll keep me hidden!

629
00:48:08,657 --> 00:48:12,577
♪ When closeness starts to stir up feelings ♪

630
00:48:12,577 --> 00:48:19,777
♪ And my heart starts to get carried away ♪

631
00:48:19,777 --> 00:48:23,177
♪ As our bond begins to change ♪

632
00:48:23,497 --> 00:48:25,537
♪ Every time I look at you ♪

633
00:48:25,537 --> 00:48:27,937
♪ My heart ♪

634
00:48:28,497 --> 00:48:31,897
♪ Flutters more than I can bear ♪

635
00:48:32,257 --> 00:48:34,977
♪ Before I knew it ♪

636
00:48:34,977 --> 00:48:37,657
♪ Before I realized how I felt ♪

637
00:48:37,657 --> 00:48:40,977
♪ I couldn't stop it anymore ♪

638
00:48:40,977 --> 00:48:44,217
♪ It's too late now ♪

639
00:48:44,217 --> 00:48:49,857
♪ I'm already yours ♪

640
00:48:51,857 --> 00:48:55,497
♪ Somehow I gave my heart to you ♪

641
00:48:55,497 --> 00:49:01,177
♪ I don't even know when it happened ♪

642
00:49:02,577 --> 00:49:05,897
♪ Someone who's always here ♪

643
00:49:05,897 --> 00:49:10,857
♪ Someone you know so well ♪

644
00:49:11,337 --> 00:49:16,737
♪ There's something I've been waiting to say ♪

645
00:49:16,737 --> 00:49:22,177
♪ But I don't know how to say it ♪

646
00:49:24,497 --> 00:49:28,097
♪ Being by your side like this ♪

647
00:49:28,097 --> 00:49:32,257
♪ Makes me feel so good that I still... ♪
